==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=kicker}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkɪkɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-kicker.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪkə(r)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{-er|kick}}

The southern-U.S. sense referring to a person derives from {{m|en|shit-kicker}}, referring to a cowboy with boots used to kick away cow manure.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[kick|kicks]].
# {{context|sports|lang=en}} One who takes kicks.
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} The [[kicking strap]].
# {{context|nautical|informal|lang=en}} An [[outboard motor]].
# {{context|colloquial|lang=en}} An unexpected [[situation]], [[detail]] or circumstance, often [[unpleasant]].
#: ''John wants to climb the wall, but the '''kicker''' is that it is thirty feet tall.''
#: ''Tuition is free; the '''kicker''' is that mandatory room and board costs twice as much as at other colleges.''
# {{context|finance|lang=en}} An enticement for investors, e.g. [[warranty]] added to the investment contract.
# {{context|poker|lang=en}} An [[unpaired]] [[card]] which is part of a [[pair]], [[two pair]], or [[three of a kind]] poker hand.
#: ''Jill's hand was two pair, aces and sevens, with a king '''kicker'''.''
# {{context|slang|Southern US|lang=en}} A particular type of [[Texan]] who is associated with [[country]]/[[western]] attire, attitudes{{,}} and/or philosophy.
# {{context|journalism|lang=en}} The last one or two paragraphs of a story.

